codemap 8
path feature-path-add
kind flow
author ai
group features/cli
note path-add <name> <sym|file start end> [under]: add one step to a path. A lone target is a symbol name and the step covers the whole symbol; a file with a start and end (1-based, inclusive) pins that line range. under is the index of the parent step as paths prints it, -1 for a root step; without it the step goes under the last step in the list, so consecutive adds build a chain. The step is recorded with the caller's author (ai from the CLI). In a flow the command also says when the parent does not call the new step, because a flow is meant to read as a call tree and the tool does not enforce that any other way.

